From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 11:28:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lane-298 item 5 prefetch-ahead: one PrefetchVirtualMemory
 over each ubatch's PLE row pages (LLAMA_PLE_PREFETCH=1 opt-in)

Novel-text prefill r1 runs -28% vs the repeat (pleio2: cold PLE row pages take one serial hard fault each inside the CPU gather). llama_mmap::prefetch_rows batches the ubatch's row pages (sorted, deduped, adjacent pages merged) into one PrefetchVirtualMemory call before compute. Opt-in until run-pfa.ps1 reads; =2 also prefetches decode; LLAMA_PLE_PREFETCH_PLANT=1 shifts rows by half the table as the planted RED. WARN receipt per multi-token ubatch: tokens, pages, call ms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Lane: lane-298
(cherry picked from commit 98017585ff1f37646a1b8d5efe1ba2739e49aa95)

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - fork-authored (lane-298); no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: part of win W13, PLE prefetch-ahead (one PrefetchVirtualMemory per ubatch): novel 2,000-token prefill 126.01 -> 180.15 t/s (+42.9%), decode r1 +6.21%, repeat prefill +1.14%; MEANS of 4 requests; plant RED +2.02%; off2 tainted, off1 alone 126.00 -> 180.10; cells/pfa-10051313-* (state head = 6b0e35cf52) [release ledger Table 1 W13]
